1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:02,800
Type one sentence, and your AI designs a

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,980
real part you can 3D print.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,360
You don't need to know CAD.

4
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:08,670
It's called text-to-cad:

5
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:11,040
free, open source, and 19,000 stars on

6
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:11,700
GitHub.

7
00:00:12,090 --> 00:00:13,220
It isn't a website.

8
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:14,900
It's a plugin for your AI agent:

9
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:16,600
Claude Code, Codex, Cursor,

10
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:17,610
Gemini or Grok.

11
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:19,830
You don't even install it yourself.

12
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:21,050
You tell your agent:

13
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:23,380
install text-to-cad, and paste the link.

14
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:25,150
Then you just ask:

15
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:26,420
a wall bracket for a shelf,

16
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:28,840
40 mm wide, with two screw holes.

17
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:31,030
Your agent writes a short Python script,

18
00:00:31,050 --> 00:00:32,370
and that script is the part.

19
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:34,390
You can spin it around right in the chat.

20
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:36,220
Every size is a number.

21
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:37,990
Change the width from 40 to 60,

22
00:00:38,030 --> 00:00:40,200
run it again, and the whole part updates.

23
00:00:40,590 --> 00:00:42,150
Out comes a real CAD file:

24
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,930
STEP for engineering software,

25
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:47,000
or STL and 3MF for your 3D printer.

26
00:00:47,410 --> 00:00:49,530
It also works from a photo or a sketch,

27
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:50,740
and pulls real screws,

28
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:52,990
bearings and motors from a parts library.

29
00:00:53,390 --> 00:00:55,340
Before you print, it checks the design:

30
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:56,690
walls too thin to print,

31
00:00:56,710 --> 00:00:58,230
and overhangs that need support.

32
00:00:58,710 --> 00:01:00,970
It draws dimensioned engineering drawings,

33
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:02,600
slices the model into G-code,

34
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:04,440
and can send it to a Bambu Lab printer.

35
00:01:04,830 --> 00:01:06,400
It even writes the files that describe a

36
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:09,660
robot, and reviews parts for CNC machining

37
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:10,690
and sheet metal.

38
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:12,760
The catch: by default it sends usage

39
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:14,830
stats, never your files or prompts.

40
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:16,570
One command turns that off.

41
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:18,270
And on Windows 11,

42
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:19,900
Smart App Control can block its CAD

43
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,660
engine. Turning that off is one-way,

44
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:23,570
so WSL is the safer route.

45
00:01:24,030 --> 00:01:25,670
Your AI just learned CAD.

46
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:27,050
That's today's tool.

47
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:28,910
There's a new one every day.
